infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two directions a dependency can point
  desc Same modules, opposite consequences — concrete depends on abstract, never the reverse
  compares
    - label Concrete → concrete (violates the rule)
      children
        - label Imports a volatile module
          desc Billing imports PostgresOrderRepository, an implementation detail
        - label Changes cascade upward
          desc Any repo internal change forces billing to recompile and recheck
        - label Billing sits in the blast radius
          desc Volatility propagates up the import chain
        - label Extraction carries the whole platform
          desc The transitive import closure spans every module
    - label Concrete → abstract (follows the rule)
      children
        - label Imports a stable contract
          desc Billing imports IOrderRepository; the repo implements it
        - label Changes stay isolated
          desc The repository can change freely while the contract holds
        - label Billing leaves the blast radius
          desc It depends only on the interface, not the implementation
        - label Extraction moves billing + its interfaces
          desc The transitive closure is just the contracts it depends on
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
